# handsoff-loop Slice DF amendment — non-tech-user-framed candidate designs

2026-06-24. An owner-directed amendment to the sealed Slice DF (design-first
front stage) per docs/plans/handsoff-design-first-and-build-heartbeat.md §5
(AC.DF.6). Empirically motivated: a live rehearsal generated candidate
designs framed as a command-line tool and a "file-watch daemon" — developer
machinery the target non-technical user (a small-firm owner) cannot operate.
The design-generation must assume a non-technical user by default and produce
candidates the user can actually SEE, understand, and choose between.

MOTIVE (prime directive, Lens 0). The user brings WHAT they want in THEIR
terms; loam owns HOW; the design they review must be in their vocabulary
(visible outcomes), never the machinery. Rehearsal-1 surfaced this defect
cheaply, before the room — which is the rehearsal's purpose.

Single-component fence on the workspace-bootstrap anchor (the handsoff-loop
family's seal anchor — source under framework/tools/handsoff-loop/, inside
the workspace-bootstrap seal-test's admitted framework/tools/ prefix; same
pattern as the Slice DF / Slice HB seals).

Change (generative.py):

  - NEW: generate_candidate_designs gains a user_tech_level parameter
    (DEFAULT "non_technical" — the owner ruling + the demo case). The
    candidate space is framed for the tech level: a non-tech user draws
    direction seeds ONLY from see-and-use / sensible-delivery families (no
    CLI / daemon / drop-folder seed); a technical user gets the full seed
    set (the constraint is "infer level, constrain space", NOT hardcode
    web-only).
  - NEW: a tech-level prompt constraint — for a non-tech user the
    per-candidate prompt forbids the developer-machinery surfaces and demands
    a candidate stating what the user PERSONALLY does + what the OUTPUT looks
    like (a visible/interactive experience OR a sensible automated delivery,
    e.g. the finished result emailed on a schedule).
  - NEW: is_nontech_operable(form_factor, tool_plan) — a held-out STRUCTURAL
    classifier (domain-blind, prompt-blind) that drops any candidate whose
    primary interaction reads as a CLI / daemon / background-watch /
    drop-folder surface, UNLESS the same text clearly names a
    visible/delivery affordance (a scheduled EMAIL report is operable). For a
    non-tech user the candidate loop applies this filter, so the user is
    NEVER surfaced a candidate they cannot operate even if the model ignores
    the prompt. The classifier never sees the generation prompt — it is the
    falsifiable AC.DF.6 check.
  - UNCHANGED: the single-design generate_design path; the AC.GEN.2
    domain-blindness (the classifier keys on interaction-surface vocabulary,
    NOT any business domain — the rehearsal's domain context is named only in
    the AC.DF.6 test + the plan-doc, never in source); the
    choose_design_fn=None non-interactive S6 path (no user_tech_level is
    passed at the call site, so the default non-tech framing flows through
    without touching build_from_intent.py).

AC surface:

  - AC.DF.6 — candidate designs are framed for the user's tech level
    (defaulting NON-TECHNICAL); a non-tech user is never offered a candidate
    whose primary interaction is developer machinery. Verified by a held-out
    structural classifier the generator never saw + an outcome-altitude live
    test (env-gated) that runs a real generation over the rehearsal ask and
    asserts every surfaced candidate is non-tech operable.

Method-level choices are the builder's call per ODD §1.1: the two-layer
enforcement (seed partition + prompt constraint at generation; held-out
classifier at filter) gives the non-tech user a clean candidate set even if
one layer slips. A technical user keeps the full machinery space (the
follow-up: inferring the tech level upstream so a CONFIRMED technical user
gets technical candidates — the demo case is non-tech and is covered by the
default).

Out of scope: inferring the user's tech level upstream in intake (the default
non-tech covers the demo + the owner ruling; the technical-user inference is a
surfaced follow-up); a clickable mockup; changing the build / freeze / verify
spine; pushing to origin (owner-gated — LOCAL seal only).

